<script>
import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={['/ai/assistant', '/ai/pairing', '/app/on-pairing', '/cli/bridge']}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/assistant.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('both providers play one conversation as one event sequence, tools called as the asker — 44.2, 44.7, 44.17'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/assistant/lib/ClaudeApiRequest.test.ts',
            from: ["test('the body is sent as written, with the transcript'"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/assistant.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a permission prompt is answered by the paired page alone — 44.81, 44.83'",
            ],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Run the CRM assistant on the Claude API">
        <p>Pass <code>provider.claudeApi</code> a Messages API request body and your key. abide
            adds <code>messages</code> and <code>stream</code>, and sends every other field as
            written.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { provider } from '@abide/abide/server'

            const claude = provider.claudeApi({
                apiKey: Bun.env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY ?? '',
                model: 'claude-opus-5',
                max_tokens: 1024,
                system: 'Answer questions about contacts.',
            })
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Run the turn on the visitor's own Claude Code">
        <p>With <code>provider.claudeCode</code>, the conversation runs on the asker's machine,
            on their own plan. Asking with no bridge paired is refused 409.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { provider } from '@abide/abide/server'

            const claudeCode = provider.claudeCode({
                systemPrompt: 'Answer in one sentence.',
                tools: ['WebSearch'],
            })
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Answer the permission prompt a turn waits on">
        <p>A tool Claude Code would ask about arrives as a <code>permission</code> event. Send the
            visitor's answer back through a handler calling <code>provider.claudeCode.permit</code>.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { provider, rpc } from '@abide/abide/server'

            export default rpc(
                ({ id, allow }: { id: string; allow: boolean }) =>
                    provider.claudeCode.permit(id, allow),
                { methods: ['POST'], clients: { mcp: false } },
            )
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Read the visitor's calendar with no model">
        <p>Where the server already knows the call, <code>provider.claudeCode.callTool</code> runs
            one MCP tool of the visitor's machine. A bridge that can make the call itself asks no
            model.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { provider } from '@abide/abide/server'

            const { content, failed } = await provider.claudeCode.callTool(
                'mcp__calendar__meetings',
                { day: 'today' },
            )
        `} />
    </Section>
</Doc>
